otnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-44/omp-44/cells/with/trig-omp-multistep/29/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.3.0 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/d3e08e91b65a46fc6d88bbb8ba641b6047172ce5/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Bug: `to_cents` truncates float error (`19.99*100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 1998). Fix: round to nearest cent.\npytest isn't installed, so I'm running the test functions directly.\nI fixed the bug in `ledger/currency.py`. `to_cents` was converting prices with `int(amount * 100)`, which chops off the decimals. Floats can't store most prices exactly, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999\u2026` and became 1998 cents instead of 1999. The same thing happened with 0.29, which became 28 cents. Every subtotal, tax and total was built on those cent values, so all of them were wrong.\n\nThe fix changes it to `round(amount * 100)`. That's enough for prices with at most two decimal places, which is what the tests use. For a price with fractions of a cent, `round` sends an exact half to the nearest even number rather than always up. If you need such prices to always round half up, the fix would be to convert them with `Decimal` instead.\n\npytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with python3. All 4 tests in `test_totals.py` and the one in `test_report.py` pass.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "repl